	(text_box "U501 MCXA153VLH (LQFP64): every pin"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 140 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "10c57520-bbb5-55a1-ac17-016438789ab9")
	)
	(text_box "Pin numbers and names from NXP Table 41 (LQFP64 column). The three consent clocks (HOLD_S_CLK, PERMIT_CLK, TEST_PERMIT_CLK)\nare plain GPIOs toggled by the control loop (F-1); the same pins also carry CTIMER1 match outputs for a one-pulse variant,\nnever a free-running timer. Ports are 3.3 V only: VDIO max = VDD + 0.3 V (Table 8); only P3_27/P3_28 are 5 V tolerant and\nthey are unused.\nWake-capable inputs (WUU0) are used for SEQ_ACT_S_N, SEQ_DONE_S_N, OVP_TRIP, CANCEL_S_N, SBZ_INT_N and the link receiver.\nLPSPI0 = pad-impedance front end (16), LPSPI1 = voltage ADC (08), LPUART2 = link."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 140 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "08a87cac-9e38-55a9-a935-61d36ab296c8")
	)
	(text_box "U501 supply decoupling and analog supply"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.72 25.4 0)
		(size 260.11 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "20c3d88d-0117-5cc0-ab71-f8873ded1826")
	)
	(text_box "VDD: 4 pins, 100 nF each + 10 uF. VDD_ANA through a ferrite bead with 100 nF + 1 uF (VDD and VDD_ANA within 0.1 V of each other, Table 9; the bead's DC drop at the ADC's current is negligible). The ADC reference VREFH is bonded to\nVDD_ANA in this package, so the NTC bias is taken from VDDA_S (ratiometric). VDD_USB unused: 10 kOhm to GND as Table 42 recommends; USB0_DP/DM float. The datasheet gives no decoupling figure: values are common practice [EST]\n(capture notes)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.72 31.75 0)
		(size 260.11 8.477)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1ab7a0e-e34a-5a5b-9214-9bec40079c5e")
	)
	(text_box "Supervisor's own 16 MHz crystal (§B2.4)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 466.15 25.4 0)
		(size 140 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3b21505d-7e44-530a-be43-92aba5edf6f7")
	)
	(text_box "ECX-32 16 MHz, CL 10 pF, ESR <= 80 Ohm (inside Table 24's 16 MHz examples, Rm 80-200 Ohm). Load caps 12 pF C0G: CL =\n12*12/(12+12) + Cstray (EXTAL/XTAL pin parasitics 2 pF typ each, about 1 pF in series, + ~2 pF board) = 9-10 pF. Different\ncrystal maker from the main controller's (Abracon) so a batch defect cannot stop both clocks (D-39 spirit)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 466.15 31.75 0)
		(size 140 8.477)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
