	)
	(text_box "Over-voltage latch reset and self-test injection (issue 3: OVP_RST, OVP_TEST to sheet 08)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.72 160.875 0)
		(size 154.52 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4f272768-b242-5f82-a787-0316aebb00ec")
	)
	(text_box "OVP_RST (P3_12) and OVP_TEST (P3_13): push-pull GPIOs on 3V3_SUP, input buffer disabled and not driven from reset (Table 41 'Default -\nDIS'), so the 100 kOhm pull-downs on 08 hold both low = no reset edge, no injection. OVP_RST is AC-coupled on 08 into 100 nF (C812):\ndriven straight from the pin, the first instant of each edge would be limited only by the pin's own output resistance (VOL <= 0.5 V at 4\nmA, Table 11, i.e. up to ~125 Ohm; typical lower), above the 25 mA single-pin limit of Table 8. R518 220 Ohm limits it to <= 3.3 V / 220\nOhm = 15 mA [CALC]. It slows the edge into C812 to tau = 220 Ohm x 100 nF = 22 us, so a reset pulse must be >= 100 us (4.5 tau: the\nBSS138 gate on 08 reaches >= 3.2 V) instead of the contract's >= 10 us (capture notes, problem P-1). OVP_TEST drives 22 kOhm + a BAS116\non 08 (<= 0.12 mA): no series resistor needed. OVP_TEST left high latches OVP_TRIP, which forces both discharge paths on: a stuck pin\nfails towards \"cannot charge\", not towards a shock."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.72 167.225 0)
		(size 154.52 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "833aa61b-574b-564a-b31d-010825641c34")
	)
	(text_box "Supervisor's own alarm: piezo sounder driven as a bridge, and a red fault light (D-26)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 360.56 160.875 0)
		(size 239.95 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b454d42-b575-592f-83a9-9e5bc6d8b84d")
	)
	(text_box "U504 dual Schmitt buffer on 3V3_SUP drives the sounder differentially from the complementary pair PWM0_A0/B0 (P3_6/P3_7): 6.6 V peak-to-peak across the element from a 3.3 V rail. 100 kOhm pull-downs hold both\ninputs low (silent) while U501 is in reset; 33 Ohm per side limits the charging current of the element's capacitance. Fault light: red LED from a high-drive pad (P3_0) through 220 Ohm. Both are off by default and\nswitched on by firmware (set_fault_alarm). The sounder part and its loudness belong to WP-C (contract §9) and are provisional here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 360.56 167.225 0)
		(size 239.95 8.477)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "084971ad-9b16-5dbe-95dc-80885a96f795")
	)
	(text_box "Supply nodes fed through a ferrite bead or 0 Ohm link: PWR_FLAG tells ERC they are driven on purpose (permanent, not a placeholder workaround)."
